Terraform Interview Questions – 2 to 4 Years Experience

If you have 2–4 years of experience, interviewers expect you to know how Terraform works internally, not just basic commands.

Here are must-prepare Terraform interview questions 👇

• What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and why is it important?
• Why did you choose Terraform over CloudFormation/ARM?
• How does Terraform work internally?
• What are providers in Terraform?
• What are resources and data sources?
Difference between terraform init, plan, and apply?
• What is the Terraform state file?
• Why is remote state important?
• How do you store state securely?
• Difference between local state and remote state?
• What is state locking and why is it needed?
• What are Terraform modules?
• How do you structure Terraform code for large projects?
• Difference between count and for_each?
• What are variables and outputs?
• What are locals in Terraform?
• What is terraform.tfvars?
• What is dependency graph in Terraform?
• What is depends_on and when do you use it?
What are workspaces and their use cases?
• How do you manage multiple environments (dev, stage, prod)?
• What is terraform refresh?
• What is drift detection in Terraform?
• How do you import existing resources into Terraform?
• What is terraform taint and when is it used?
• How do you handle secrets in Terraform?
• How do you manage Terraform code in CI/CD pipelines?
• What happens if the state file is deleted or corrupted?
• How do you troubleshoot a failed terraform apply?
• What Terraform challenges have you faced in your project?

Interview Tip (2–4 yrs):
Be ready to explain your Terraform folder structure, state backend, and how you handled changes safely in production.

